  "description": "A single long-wave pulse launched by a sudden paddle displacement, propagating over a shelf and running up a slope.",
  "approximation": "TIER 2 -- THIS IS A LONG-WAVE PROPAGATION EXPERIMENT, NOT A TSUNAMI MODEL. A real tsunami is a hundreds-of-kilometre wave over ocean-depth bathymetry with Coriolis and dispersive effects over hours of propagation; this is a metre-scale flume pulse over a ramp lasting seconds. It demonstrates how a solitary long wave shoals and runs up. Nothing here transfers to any real coastline, and no inundation number from it should be quoted as a hazard estimate.",
